Open GPUI iOS backend

Derived from the Apache-2.0 GPUI iOS backend in Zed:
https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/tree/78f5d7446c55f6c1aa9b66e8111f6b3f4625ebb0/crates/gpui_ios

Source tree: 78f5d7446c55f6c1aa9b66e8111f6b3f4625ebb0
Latest upstream iOS change in that tree:
fdcb1981103408e63fff5ef47c8ae2f9995262ad (Low Power Mode frame pacing).
The subsequent selected rendering target is 6ceb6fee8738274589b59139df27efc191ec2231.
The official comparison between those targets changes no gpui_ios files.

The original source, examples, Info.plist and native text-input tests retain
their Apache-2.0 license. LICENSE-APACHE contains the complete regular-file
license text, replacing the upstream repository-relative symlink.

Open GPUI adaptations use extracted open_gpui_* dependency aliases, the shared
Apple renderer, native callback leases and command ingress, exact presentation
shutdown tickets, coherent window geometry, demand-driven frame scheduling and
scoped UIKit idle-sleep inhibition. The simulator packager is a Python
replacement for the upstream Bash helper.
